      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's definitely better, the weight is starting to feel more \"centerpiece.\" I like the line about the world remembering how to bleed.\n\nStill, the depth score is still hovering in a zone that might trigger a \"low quality\" flag from the automatic review. We really need to get this into the 250-300 word range to be safe for the UI layout. \n\nI'm not asking you to just add fluff—I need you to actually build out the lore. Maybe describe the visual sensation of the ley lines shifting, or go into more detail about the specific moment the Shimmering Collapse happened for her. If you can make it much more descriptive and immersive like that, it should solve the word count issue naturally without it feeling like filler. Give it everything you've got.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
